TOTK: NVN2 task and mesh shaders as VK_EXT_mesh_shader stages (docs/oot-xlate.md). The Ampere code is translated as a compute
kernel with seedds/nxnative's stage memory lowering (patch 0019: ISBERD, AST 0x927; here also ISBERD mode 0xb8, a read of the
task's own output payload); IGpuAccessor.QueryMeshStage (MeshStage) describes the stage, and CodeGen/Spirv/MeshStageWrapper.cs
writes a TaskEXT / MeshEXT entry point around the kernel as nxnative's dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_meshstage.py (MIT) writes the Metal
object and mesh functions: the stage memory zeroed, the payload copied in, the workgroup number from c[0] + 0x9F0 (the
runtime's VK_C0_MESH_FIRST) plus WorkgroupId, the kernel called, then the task payload and EmitMeshTasksEXT, or
SetMeshOutputsEXT, the positions, generic and per-primitive attributes and the triangle indices. Such a module is SPIR-V
1.4: its entry point lists every global, and its storage buffers are Block in StorageBuffer (Spv.Generator gains the
SPV_EXT_mesh_shader enumerants and instructions, values from the SPIR-V registry). Every other translation is unchanged.

